# Copy to server/.env. Provider calls are made in-process (adr-007) — set a
# key per provider you want routable; models whose provider has no key fail
# instantly and the routing walk moves on.

# Free-tier MVP keys (the default routes in routing.ts run on these):
GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_...
GEMINI_API_KEY=...

# Optional paid fallbacks / BYOK providers:
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# Local Ollama (dev-only gemma3-4b fallback); default shown:
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1

# Operator-cost guardrails (adr-008); defaults shown, 0 disables one.
# BYOK requests are exempt — they spend the caller's key.
# LIMIT_GENERATIONS_PER_DAY=10
# LIMIT_REGENERATIONS_PER_DAY=30
# LIMIT_BACKGROUNDS_PER_DAY=3
# DAILY_BUDGET_USD=5

# Custom domain (docs/05-deployment.md): redirect every other host (e.g. the
# platform *.code.run endpoint) to this one. Unset = no redirect.
# CANONICAL_HOST=invinto.app

# Host sign-in with Google (adr-014). Both unset = sign-in is off and publish
# stays anonymous, which is a supported mode — local development and
# self-hosting need no OAuth client. Create credentials at
# https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials (OAuth client, type "Web
# application") and register the callback below as an authorized redirect URI.
#
# Production needs a registrable domain of your own: Google refuses any host
# that is not a top private domain, and platform preview domains like
# *.code.run are on the Public Suffix List, so they are rejected outright.
# localhost is exempt, so development works with no domain at all — register
# http://localhost:5173/api/auth/google/callback (what `pnpm dev` serves; Vite
# proxies /api without rewriting Host) and leave GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI unset.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=....apps.googleusercontent.com
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=...
#
# The callback URI is derived from the incoming request, so
# http://localhost:3001/api/auth/google/callback works in development with
# nothing set here. Set it explicitly in production: Google matches it against
# its registered allowlist, and a deployment behind CANONICAL_HOST must send
# the canonical host rather than the platform one.
# GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=https://invinto.app/api/auth/google/callback
#
# Whether a *first* publish requires an account (adr-014 §2). On by default
# once the two keys above are set; 0 disables it, following the adr-008
# convention. Republishing with a valid manage token is never gated.
#
# Set this to 0 while rolling sign-in out, so hosts can sign in before
# anonymous publishing stops working, then remove it. It is also how the ADR's
# revisit trigger is pulled: if publish-rate drops against the frozen baseline
# at GET /api/metrics, moving the gate is this flag, not a deploy.
# PUBLISH_REQUIRES_ACCOUNT=0

# RSVP notifications (adr-015). Both unset = notifications are off and every
# other feature is unchanged, following the keyless-boot precedent above: a
# deployment with no mail credentials boots, publishes and takes RSVPs
# normally, and nothing in the UI offers a preference that cannot be honoured.
# GET /healthz reports notifications.configured.
#
# Only a signed-in host's invitations can notify at all (§1) — the address is
# the Google-verified one from sign-in, so this does nothing without the OAuth
# credentials above.
#
# NOTIFY_FROM must be on a domain verified with the provider, with its SPF and
# DKIM records published. An unverified sender is not an error you will see in
# the logs — the API returns 200 and the mail lands in spam.
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
# NOTIFY_FROM=INVITO <replies@invinto.app>
#
# At most one email per invitation per window (§4); default shown. The first
# reply mails immediately, replies inside the window mail nothing, and the next
# one after it carries the count since the last notification. 0 notifies on
# every reply — a 100-guest wedding is then 100 emails to one host.
# NOTIFY_WINDOW_MINUTES=60

# PORT=3001
